From 5d12ccf916c80f6a3f4f3b4e738b656cebed1d49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Jul 2026 18:16:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ui: fix Captive Portal JS corruption from theme bake +
 visual-audit fixes

Full visual parity audit (113 pages x stock-vs-reaper screenshots, reviewed
pairwise): 8 pages had defects, all fixed or triaged:

- CRITICAL: Captive_Portal.asp / Captive_Portal_Advanced.asp - the UI-flip
  bake injected the theme <link>+bounce before the FIRST </head>, which on
  these two pages sits INSIDE a JavaScript splash-page template string
  (html_landing / splash_page_adv_html). The raw quotes+newlines were a JS
  syntax error in the shipped builds and the real document head never got
  the theme (pages rendered fully stock). Repaired the template strings and
  re-injected before the real (last) </head>. Swept all other pages: no
  other multi-</head> victims.
- AiProtection MaliciousSites/IPS/InfectedDevice (+_m): Security Event /
  Threat Activities cards + events table paint grey via INLINE style
  attributes - now matched with [style*=...] selectors (bgcolor rules never
  applied to these)
- Notification page Reminds box: shared .control_bg grey panel -> dark
- Captive Portal panels: .gn_content, splash textarea/toolbar/step classes
- QoS user rules: FormTable thead gradient moved from td to tr so multi-td
  header rows no longer restart the gradient per cell
Known-low (not fixed): Main_Analysis latency-chart canvas draws at stock
740px width inside the wider themed panel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/Captive_Portal.asp     |  6 +++---
 .../router/www/Captive_Portal_Advanced.asp    |  6 +++---
 .../src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css  | 21 ++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

